  "text": "Homepage - consortium of Uganda university libraries Consortium of Uganda University Libraries (CUUL) Home About About CUUL Executive Committee Functional Committee Heads CUUL Gallery Contact Online Library Databases Databases A-Z Open Access Resources EIFL Resources Downloads Repositories Mak IR Repository (Post Graduate) Dissertations (Under Graduate) Search Engines Libhub/Kiox Research 4 Life Google Scholar MyLoft About MyLoft MyLoft Guide MyLoft Signup Members Public Universities Private Universities Affiliate Members Apply To CUUL Support CUUL CUUL Journal Webmail About MyLoft Signup to MyLoft MyLoft Guide Support CUUL Home About About CUUL Executive Committee Functional Committee Heads CUUL Gallery Contact Online Library Databases Databases A-Z Open Access Resources EIFL Resources Downloads Repositories Mak IR Repository (Post Graduate) Dissertations (Under Graduate) Search Engines Libhub/Kiox Research 4 Life Google Scholar MyLoft About MyLoft MyLoft Guide MyLoft Signup Members Public Universities Private Universities Affiliate Members Apply To CUUL Support CUUL CUUL Journal Webmail Vision A sustainable, collaborative, and innovative knowledge ecosystem that strengthens research and academic libraries for societal development. Mission “To empower research and academic libraries to enhance research, learning, and innovative solutions for sustainable societal development.” Find Us on tiktok CUUL is now on tiktok. visit our page to know more about CUUL activities. Discover More Follow us on Twitter Follow our page on twitter and keep up to date with CUUL activities Follow our page Quick Links MyLoft Guide Databases 5th CUUL ANNUAL CONFERENCE SDGs Acceleration Actions Downloads FAQs CUUL Profile Welcome to CUUL The Consortium of Uganda University Libraries (CUUL) is a non-profit organization established to plan and manage projects and activities collaboratively in order to provide member library communities with efficient and effective access to vital research information resources. Please note that we are still open and welcoming new eligible members. Visit our about us page for more details Apply Now Support CUUL to grow CUUL is looking for partners to support its activities and achieve the objectives set out. Click link above to find out more New Member Applications are now open About CUUL Established on 14th December 2001. The purpose of the Consortium is to facilitate effective and efficient collaboration and resource sharing among member libraries in Uganda. The Secretariat is at Makerere University Business School (MUBS) Learn More CUUL Activities The Consortium generally initiates and coordinates projects and activities related to resource sharing and Library networking and maintain cooperative relationships with groups or agencies with similar goals. Learn More Becoming A Member All University Libraries in Uganda, both public and licensed private, plus other licensed degree awarding institutions in Uganda are members of CUUL on payment of Membership fees. Learn More Benefits to Members Member Libraries become an information rich educational institute; promote and advance teaching and learning; facilitate improved productivity and quality of research cost effectively. Learn More CUUL Partners News & Events Read All News October 1, 2026 Conferences 5TH CUUL ANNUAL CONFERENCE Read More June 23, 2026 News ULIA Workshop Read More June 23, 2026 Conferences CUUL AGM Read More 0 Years of CUUL Existance 0 Public Universities 0 Private Universities 0 Affiliate Members Video Tour of CUUL activities Address Makerere University Business School cuuladmin@cuul.or.ug +256703815721 | +256-772985720 View on Google Important Links AJLII E-books Databases A-Z EIFL Resources Lib/Kiox Google Scholar Research 4 Life Our Partners KLISC TLA eifl ULIA RENU EBSCO HOST Social Networks X Youtube Tiktok Copyright All Right Reserved 2026, CUUL",
